{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MrJ2Ksjw8DmZPBPaVPBsG6","type":"tool_result","content":"/workspace/investigation/ideas/03_parametric_exposure_mapping_family_with_bic_gated_switch_from_linear_regression_for_gate/program_1/:\nanalysis\ncorrect.json\nevaluation_evidence.json\nevaluation_manifest.json\nharness_evaluate_stderr.log\nharness_evaluate_stdout.log\nmetrics.json\nprogram_spec.toml\nrubric_status.json\nsrc\n\n/workspace/investigation/ideas/03_parametric_exposure_mapping_family_with_bic_gated_switch_from_linear_regression_for_gate/program_1/src:\nprogram.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Regression-based GATE estimator under network interference (starter candidate).\n     2\t\n     3\tInterface: ``python_rpc_v1:handle``.  ``handle(request) -> response`` takes and returns\n     4\tfinite JSON-compatible values only.  The candidate owns all of its state in memory; it\n     5\tshares no filesystem with the evaluator and must not read or write evaluator paths.\n     6\t\n     7\tOperations\n     8\t----------\n     9\t``{\"op\": \"reset\", \"seed\": <int >= 0>}``\n    10\t    Clears ALL candidate state and seeds the candidate RNG.  The seed only initializes\n    11\t    randomness; it never identifies a plane, case or workload.  Any non-negative integer\n    12\t    is valid.  Response: exactly ``{\"ok\": true}`` (no other keys).\n    13\t\n    14\t``{\"op\": \"estimate\", ...}``\n    15\t    One full dataset from one randomized experiment on a network.  The evaluator sends\n    16\t    exactly one ``reset`` per episode and then four ``estimate`` requests in an\n    17\t    evaluator-private order.  All four have the identical format and size and the same\n    18\t    budget; the candidate must treat every request as an ordinary dataset and must not\n    19\t    try to detect which one is which.  Each ``estimate`` is independent: return the best\n    20\t    estimate for the request in hand.\n    21\t\n    22\t    Request fields (all present, no others):\n    23\t      op         \"estimate\"\n    24\t      n          int, number of nodes (nodes are 0..n-1)\n    25\t      edges      array object, undirected unique edges (u < v), dtype int32, shape [E, 2]\n    26\t      covariates array object, node covariates, dtype float64, shape [n, 2]\n    27\t      treatment  array object, realized treatment assignment, dtype uint8 (0/1), shape [n]\n    28\t      outcomes   array object, observed outcomes, dtype float64, shape [n]\n    29\t      design     {\"kind\": \"bernoulli\" | \"cluster\",\n    30\t                  \"probability\": float,   # marginal treatment probability of the design\n    31\t                  \"cluster_labels\": array object (int32, shape [n]) or null}\n    32\t                 \"bernoulli\": each node treated independently with ``probability``.\n    33\t                 \"cluster\":   whole clusters (``cluster_labels``) are treated together;\n    34\t                              exactly round(K*probability) of the K clusters are treated,\n    35\t                              chosen uniformly at random.\n    36\t      workload   {\"max_op_seconds\": float,  # soft per-request time budget (hard cap is a\n    37\t                                            # little larger; exceeding it fails the episode)\n    38\t                  \"ci_level\": float}        # nominal level of the requested interval\n    39\t\n    40\t    Array objects are ``{\"dtype\": \"<name>\", \"shape\": [...], \"encoding\": \"base64-le\",\n    41\t    \"data\": \"<base64 of the C-order little-endian buffer>\"}``; see ``decode_array``.\n    42\t\n    43\t    Target: the global average treatment effect (GATE), i.e. the mean over nodes of\n    44\t    Y_i(all nodes treated) - Y_i(all nodes control) for the (hidden) potential outcomes.\n    45\t    The interference mechanism, its parameters and the true GATE are never revealed.\n    46\t\n    47\t    Response (JSON object): required keys ``estimate``, ``ci_low``, ``ci_high``\n    48\t    (finite numbers with ci_low <= estimate <= ci_high); optional key ``diagnostics``\n    49\t    (a JSON object, at most 4096 bytes serialized; ignored for scoring).  Any other key,\n    50\t    a non-finite number, a malformed type or an interval that does not contain the\n    51\t    estimate makes that request invalid (the episode keeps its worst-case contribution).\n    52\t\n    53\tLimits (enforced by the evaluator; a violation is a failed request, never retried):\n    54\t  * ``reset`` must answer within 4 s (it includes process/import start-up);\n    55\t  * each ``estimate`` must answer within 3 s wall clock (``workload.max_op_seconds`` = 2.5 s\n    56\t    is the soft budget to aim for); at most 4 threads of CPU are available;\n    57\t  * a complete request is below 0.5 MiB and a complete response must stay far below the\n    58\t    64 MiB wire limit (a valid response is < 5 KiB);\n    59\t  * no filesystem or network is shared with the evaluator; do not read or write evaluator paths.\n    60\tDeterminism: all candidate randomness must derive from the ``reset`` seed, because the evaluator\n    61\treplays one episode after a fresh ``reset`` and requires the primary estimate to agree to 1e-6\n    62\t(relative to max(1, |estimate|)).\n    63\t\n    64\tScoring (evaluator-owned): per episode relative error min(|estimate - GATE| / |GATE|, 2),\n    65\ta failed/invalid request counts as 2 (and as \"not covered\" with worst-case width);\n    66\tRMSE over seeds per case, mean over the 8 cases, ``combined_score`` = -that mean.\n    67\tThe evaluator additionally runs matched negative controls (permuted outcomes, node-relabelled\n    68\tgraph, constant outcome) through the same operation; a constant-outcome request must\n    69\treturn an estimate within 1e-4 of 0, and the run must be deterministic given the reset seed.\n    70\t\"\"\"\n    71\t\n    72\timport base64\n    73\t\n    74\timport numpy as np\n    75\timport scipy.sparse as sp\n    76\t\n    77\t_STATE = {\"rng\": None, \"seed\": None}\n    78\t\n    79\t_DTYPES = {\"int32\": \"<i4\", \"float64\": \"<f8\", \"uint8\": \"u1\"}\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\tdef decode_array(obj):\n    83\t    \"\"\"Decode an array object (see module docstring) into a numpy array.\"\"\"\n    84\t    if obj is None:\n    85\t        return None\n    86\t    if obj[\"encoding\"] != \"base64-le\" or obj[\"dtype\"] not in _DTYPES:\n    87\t        raise ValueError(\"unsupported array encoding\")\n    88\t    buf = base64.b64decode(obj[\"data\"])\n    89\t    return np.frombuffer(buf, dtype=np.dtype(_DTYPES[obj[\"dtype\"]])).reshape(obj[\"shape\"]).copy()\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\tdef _adjacency(n, edges):\n    93\t    if len(edges) == 0:\n    94\t        return sp.csr_matrix((n, n))\n    95\t    u, v = edges[:, 0], edges[:, 1]\n    96\t    rows = np.concatenate([u, v])\n    97\t    cols = np.concatenate([v, u])\n    98\t    return sp.csr_matrix((np.ones(len(rows)), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n    99\t\n   100\t\n   101\tdef _features(adj, deg, z, x, treated_all):\n   102\t    \"\"\"Design matrix [1, own treatment, neighbour-treated fraction, covariates].\"\"\"\n   103\t    if treated_all is None:\n   104\t        frac = (adj @ z) / np.maximum(deg, 1.0)\n   105\t        own = z\n   106\t    else:\n   107\t        frac = np.where(deg > 0, float(treated_all), 0.0)\n   108\t        own = np.full(len(z), float(treated_all))\n   109\t    return np.column_stack([np.ones(len(z)), own, frac, x])\n   110\t\n   111\t\n   112\tdef _parse(request):\n   113\t    n = int(request[\"n\"])\n   114\t    edges = decode_array(request[\"edges\"])\n   115\t    x = decode_array(request[\"covariates\"])\n   116\t    z = decode_array(request[\"treatment\"]).astype(np.float64)\n   117\t    y = decode_array(request[\"outcomes\"])\n   118\t    adj = _adjacency(n, edges)\n   119\t    deg = np.asarray(adj.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n   120\t    return n, x, z, y, adj, deg\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\tZCRIT = 1.959963984540054  # normal quantile for ci_level = 0.95 (the only level requested)\n   124\t\n   125\t\n   126\tdef _exposure_states(adj, deg, z):\n   127\t    \"\"\"Exposure summaries for the observed, all-treated and all-control worlds.\n   128\t\n   129\t    Two-hop quantities use repeated sparse matrix-vector products only (never adj @ adj).\n   130\t    \"\"\"\n   131\t    n = len(z)\n   132\t    ones = np.ones(n)\n   133\t    walks2 = adj @ (adj @ ones)  # number of length-2 walks starting at each node\n   134\t    s1 = adj @ z\n   135\t    obs = {\n   136\t        \"own\": z,\n   137\t        \"s1\": s1,\n   138\t        \"f1\": s1 / np.maximum(deg, 1.0),\n   139\t        \"f2\": (adj @ (adj @ z)) / np.maximum(walks2, 1.0),\n   140\t    }\n   141\t    all1 = {\n   142\t        \"own\": ones,\n   143\t        \"s1\": deg.astype(np.float64),\n   144\t        \"f1\": (deg > 0).astype(np.float64),\n   145\t        \"f2\": (walks2 > 0).astype(np.float64),\n   146\t    }\n   147\t    all0 = {\"own\": np.zeros(n), \"s1\": np.zeros(n), \"f1\": np.zeros(n), \"f2\": np.zeros(n)}\n   148\t    return obs, all1, all0\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\tdef candidate_designs(deg, x):\n   152\t    \"\"\"Library of few-parameter exposure mappings.\n   153\t\n   154\t    Returns {name: (builder, count_cols)}; builder(state) -> design matrix with columns\n   155\t    [1, own, exposure features..., (x or interactions)].  ``count_cols`` marks columns that\n   156\t    are unbounded treated-neighbour counts (all-treated values get winsorised).\n   157\t    \"\"\"\n   158\t    n = len(deg)\n   159\t    pos = deg[deg > 0]\n   160\t    median_deg = max(float(np.median(pos)), 1.0) if len(pos) else 1.0\n   161\t    mean_deg = max(float(np.mean(deg)), 1.0)\n   162\t    ld = np.log1p(deg)\n   163\t    ldc = ld - ld.mean()\n   164\t    xc = x - x.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n   165\t    one = np.ones(n)\n   166\t\n   167\t    def lin(s):\n   168\t        return np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x])\n   169\t\n   170\t    specs = {\"M0_linear\": (lin, ())}\n   171\t\n   172\t    specs[\"M1_count\"] = (\n   173\t        lambda s: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"s1\"] / mean_deg, x]),\n   174\t        (2,),\n   175\t    )\n   176\t    specs[\"M2_twohop\"] = (\n   177\t        lambda s: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], s[\"f2\"], x]),\n   178\t        (),\n   179\t    )\n   180\t    specs[\"M3_interact\"] = (\n   181\t        lambda s: np.column_stack(\n   182\t            [one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x, ldc, s[\"own\"] * ldc, s[\"own\"] * xc,\n   183\t             s[\"f1\"] * ldc]\n   184\t        ),\n   185\t        (),\n   186\t    )\n   187\t    specs[\"M3b_own_deg_frac_deg\"] = (\n   188\t        lambda s: np.column_stack(\n   189\t            [one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x, ldc, s[\"own\"] * ldc, s[\"f1\"] * ldc]\n   190\t        ),\n   191\t        (),\n   192\t    )\n   193\t    specs[\"M3c_frac_x\"] = (\n   194\t        lambda s: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x, s[\"f1\"] * xc]),\n   195\t        (),\n   196\t    )\n   197\t    for k in (1.0, 3.0, 8.0):\n   198\t        specs[\"M4_sat_k%g\" % k] = (\n   199\t            (lambda s, k=k: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], 1.0 - np.exp(-k * s[\"f1\"]), x])),\n   200\t            (),\n   201\t        )\n   202\t    for t in (0.25, 0.5, 0.75):\n   203\t        specs[\"M5_sig_t%g\" % t] = (\n   204\t            (lambda s, t=t: np.column_stack(\n   205\t                [one, s[\"own\"], 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(s[\"f1\"] - t) / 0.1)), x])),\n   206\t            (),\n   207\t        )\n   208\t    for k in (0.5, 1.0, 2.0):\n   209\t        specs[\"M6_satcount_k%g\" % k] = (\n   210\t            (lambda s, k=k: np.column_stack(\n   211\t                [one, s[\"own\"], 1.0 - np.exp(-s[\"s1\"] / (k * median_deg)), x])),\n   212\t            (),\n   213\t        )\n   214\t    return specs\n   215\t\n   216\t\n   217\tdef sandwich_se(x_obs, resid, contrast, n):\n   218\t    \"\"\"HC1 sandwich delta-method standard error of contrast @ beta.\"\"\"\n   219\t    bread = np.linalg.pinv(x_obs.T @ x_obs)\n   220\t    meat = (x_obs * resid[:, None] ** 2).T @ x_obs\n   221\t    cov = bread @ meat @ bread * n / max(n - x_obs.shape[1], 1)\n   222\t    return float(np.sqrt(max(contrast @ cov @ contrast, 0.0)))\n   223\t\n   224\t\n   225\tdef _fit_candidate(builder, count_cols, states, y):\n   226\t    obs, all1, all0 = states\n   227\t    n = len(y)\n   228\t    x_obs = builder(obs)\n   229\t    x1 = builder(all1)\n   230\t    x0 = builder(all0)\n   231\t    for c in count_cols:  # winsorise count-type all-treated features\n   232\t        cap = 3.0 * float(np.percentile(x_obs[:, c], 99.5))\n   233\t        if cap > 0:\n   234\t            x1[:, c] = np.minimum(x1[:, c], cap)\n   235\t    if not (np.all(np.isfinite(x_obs)) and np.all(np.isfinite(x1)) and np.all(np.isfinite(x0))):\n   236\t        return None\n   237\t    beta, _, rank, _ = np.linalg.lstsq(x_obs, y, rcond=None)\n   238\t    resid = y - x_obs @ beta\n   239\t    rss = float(resid @ resid)\n   240\t    contrast = (x1 - x0).mean(axis=0)\n   241\t    est = float(contrast @ beta)\n   242\t    se = sandwich_se(x_obs, resid, contrast, n)\n   243\t    if not (np.isfinite(est) and np.isfinite(se)):\n   244\t        return None\n   245\t    return {\"est\": est, \"se\": se, \"rss\": rss, \"p\": int(rank)}\n   246\t\n   247\t\n   248\tdef bic_gate(fits, n, y_var, bic_margin=10.0):\n   249\t    \"\"\"Keep the linear fit unless a candidate beats it by BIC > bic_margin.\n   250\t\n   251\t    Passing candidates are averaged with BIC weights.  Returns (est, se, est0, se0).\n   252\t    \"\"\"\n   253\t    base = fits[\"M0_linear\"]\n   254\t    est0, se0 = base[\"est\"], base[\"se\"]\n   255\t    floor = 1e-12 * y_var\n   256\t\n   257\t    def bic(f):\n   258\t        return n * np.log(np.maximum(f[\"rss\"] / n, floor)) + f[\"p\"] * np.log(n)\n   259\t\n   260\t    bic0 = bic(base)\n   261\t    passing = []\n   262\t    for name, f in fits.items():\n   263\t        if name == \"M0_linear\" or f is None:\n   264\t            continue\n   265\t        b = bic(f)\n   266\t        if bic0 - b > bic_margin:\n   267\t            passing.append((b, f))\n   268\t    if not passing:\n   269\t        return est0, se0, est0, se0\n   270\t    bmin = min(b for b, _ in passing)\n   271\t    w = np.array([np.exp(-0.5 * (b - bmin)) for b, _ in passing])\n   272\t    w = w / w.sum()\n   273\t    ests = np.array([f[\"est\"] for _, f in passing])\n   274\t    ses = np.array([f[\"se\"] for _, f in passing])\n   275\t    est = float(w @ ests)\n   276\t    spread = float(np.sqrt(w @ (ests - est) ** 2))\n   277\t    se = float(w @ ses) + spread\n   278\t    # sanity guard: do not stray far from the linear estimate\n   279\t    if abs(est - est0) > 3.0 * max(abs(est0), se0) or not (np.isfinite(est) and np.isfinite(se)):\n   280\t        return est0, se0, est0, se0\n   281\t    return est, se, est0, se0\n   282\t\n   283\t\n   284\tdef _estimate(request):\n   285\t    try:\n   286\t        n, x, z, y, adj, deg = _parse(request)\n   287\t        y_var = float(np.var(y))\n   288\t        if y_var == 0.0:\n   289\t            return {\"estimate\": 0.0, \"ci_low\": 0.0, \"ci_high\": 0.0}\n   290\t        states = _exposure_states(adj, deg, z)\n   291\t        fits = {}\n   292\t        for name, (builder, count_cols) in candidate_designs(deg, x).items():\n   293\t            try:\n   294\t                fits[name] = _fit_candidate(builder, count_cols, states, y)\n   295\t            except Exception:\n   296\t                fits[name] = None\n   297\t        if fits.get(\"M0_linear\") is None:\n   298\t            raise ValueError(\"linear fit failed\")\n   299\t        est, se, est0, se0 = bic_gate(fits, n, y_var, bic_margin=10.0)\n   300\t        half = ZCRIT * se + abs(est - est0)\n   301\t        if not (np.isfinite(est) and np.isfinite(half)):\n   302\t            raise ValueError(\"non-finite\")\n   303\t        return {\"estimate\": est, \"ci_low\": est - half, \"ci_high\": est + half}\n   304\t    except Exception:\n   305\t        return _estimate_linear(request)\n   306\t\n   307\t\n   308\tdef _estimate_linear(request):\n   309\t    n, x, z, y, adj, deg = _parse(request)\n   310\t\n   311\t    x_obs = _features(adj, deg, z, x, None)\n   312\t    beta, *_ = np.linalg.lstsq(x_obs, y, rcond=None)\n   313\t    resid = y - x_obs @ beta\n   314\t    # GATE = mean over nodes of prediction(all treated) - prediction(all control).\n   315\t    contrast = (_features(adj, deg, z, x, 1) - _features(adj, deg, z, x, 0)).mean(axis=0)\n   316\t    est = float(contrast @ beta)\n   317\t\n   318\t    # Heteroskedasticity-robust (HC1) sandwich interval for the linear functional.\n   319\t    bread = np.linalg.pinv(x_obs.T @ x_obs)\n   320\t    meat = (x_obs * resid[:, None] ** 2).T @ x_obs\n   321\t    cov = bread @ meat @ bread * n / max(n - x_obs.shape[1], 1)\n   322\t    se = float(np.sqrt(max(contrast @ cov @ contrast, 0.0)))\n   323\t    zcrit = 1.959963984540054  # normal quantile for ci_level = 0.95 (the only level requested)\n   324\t    return {\"estimate\": est, \"ci_low\": est - zcrit * se, \"ci_high\": est + zcrit * se}\n   325\t\n   326\t\n   327\tdef handle(request):\n   328\t    op = request.get(\"op\")\n   329\t    if op == \"reset\":\n   330\t        seed = int(request[\"seed\"])\n   331\t        _STATE[\"seed\"] = seed\n   332\t        _STATE[\"rng\"] = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n   333\t        return {\"ok\": True}\n   334\t    if op == \"estimate\":\n   335\t        return _estimate(request)\n   336\t    raise ValueError(\"unknown op\")","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9055c2ad-8868-47aa-af47-ddab8ec71d32","uuid":"40e9bb7e-fbfa-410f-8a59-5dc60f050754","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:45:05.860Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/workspace/investigation/ideas/03_parametric_exposure_mapping_family_with_bic_gated_switch_from_linear_regression_for_gate/program_1/:\nanalysis\ncorrect.json\nevaluation_evidence.json\nevaluation_manifest.json\nharness_evaluate_stderr.log\nharness_evaluate_stdout.log\nmetrics.json\nprogram_spec.toml\nrubric_status.json\nsrc\n\n/workspace/investigation/ideas/03_parametric_exposure_mapping_family_with_bic_gated_switch_from_linear_regression_for_gate/program_1/src:\nprogram.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Regression-based GATE estimator under network interference (starter candidate).\n     2\t\n     3\tInterface: ``python_rpc_v1:handle``.  ``handle(request) -> response`` takes and returns\n     4\tfinite JSON-compatible values only.  The candidate owns all of its state in memory; it\n     5\tshares no filesystem with the evaluator and must not read or write evaluator paths.\n     6\t\n     7\tOperations\n     8\t----------\n     9\t``{\"op\": \"reset\", \"seed\": <int >= 0>}``\n    10\t    Clears ALL candidate state and seeds the candidate RNG.  The seed only initializes\n    11\t    randomness; it never identifies a plane, case or workload.  Any non-negative integer\n    12\t    is valid.  Response: exactly ``{\"ok\": true}`` (no other keys).\n    13\t\n    14\t``{\"op\": \"estimate\", ...}``\n    15\t    One full dataset from one randomized experiment on a network.  The evaluator sends\n    16\t    exactly one ``reset`` per episode and then four ``estimate`` requests in an\n    17\t    evaluator-private order.  All four have the identical format and size and the same\n    18\t    budget; the candidate must treat every request as an ordinary dataset and must not\n    19\t    try to detect which one is which.  Each ``estimate`` is independent: return the best\n    20\t    estimate for the request in hand.\n    21\t\n    22\t    Request fields (all present, no others):\n    23\t      op         \"estimate\"\n    24\t      n          int, number of nodes (nodes are 0..n-1)\n    25\t      edges      array object, undirected unique edges (u < v), dtype int32, shape [E, 2]\n    26\t      covariates array object, node covariates, dtype float64, shape [n, 2]\n    27\t      treatment  array object, realized treatment assignment, dtype uint8 (0/1), shape [n]\n    28\t      outcomes   array object, observed outcomes, dtype float64, shape [n]\n    29\t      design     {\"kind\": \"bernoulli\" | \"cluster\",\n    30\t                  \"probability\": float,   # marginal treatment probability of the design\n    31\t                  \"cluster_labels\": array object (int32, shape [n]) or null}\n    32\t                 \"bernoulli\": each node treated independently with ``probability``.\n    33\t                 \"cluster\":   whole clusters (``cluster_labels``) are treated together;\n    34\t                              exactly round(K*probability) of the K clusters are treated,\n    35\t                              chosen uniformly at random.\n    36\t      workload   {\"max_op_seconds\": float,  # soft per-request time budget (hard cap is a\n    37\t                                            # little larger; exceeding it fails the episode)\n    38\t                  \"ci_level\": float}        # nominal level of the requested interval\n    39\t\n    40\t    Array objects are ``{\"dtype\": \"<name>\", \"shape\": [...], \"encoding\": \"base64-le\",\n    41\t    \"data\": \"<base64 of the C-order little-endian buffer>\"}``; see ``decode_array``.\n    42\t\n    43\t    Target: the global average treatment effect (GATE), i.e. the mean over nodes of\n    44\t    Y_i(all nodes treated) - Y_i(all nodes control) for the (hidden) potential outcomes.\n    45\t    The interference mechanism, its parameters and the true GATE are never revealed.\n    46\t\n    47\t    Response (JSON object): required keys ``estimate``, ``ci_low``, ``ci_high``\n    48\t    (finite numbers with ci_low <= estimate <= ci_high); optional key ``diagnostics``\n    49\t    (a JSON object, at most 4096 bytes serialized; ignored for scoring).  Any other key,\n    50\t    a non-finite number, a malformed type or an interval that does not contain the\n    51\t    estimate makes that request invalid (the episode keeps its worst-case contribution).\n    52\t\n    53\tLimits (enforced by the evaluator; a violation is a failed request, never retried):\n    54\t  * ``reset`` must answer within 4 s (it includes process/import start-up);\n    55\t  * each ``estimate`` must answer within 3 s wall clock (``workload.max_op_seconds`` = 2.5 s\n    56\t    is the soft budget to aim for); at most 4 threads of CPU are available;\n    57\t  * a complete request is below 0.5 MiB and a complete response must stay far below the\n    58\t    64 MiB wire limit (a valid response is < 5 KiB);\n    59\t  * no filesystem or network is shared with the evaluator; do not read or write evaluator paths.\n    60\tDeterminism: all candidate randomness must derive from the ``reset`` seed, because the evaluator\n    61\treplays one episode after a fresh ``reset`` and requires the primary estimate to agree to 1e-6\n    62\t(relative to max(1, |estimate|)).\n    63\t\n    64\tScoring (evaluator-owned): per episode relative error min(|estimate - GATE| / |GATE|, 2),\n    65\ta failed/invalid request counts as 2 (and as \"not covered\" with worst-case width);\n    66\tRMSE over seeds per case, mean over the 8 cases, ``combined_score`` = -that mean.\n    67\tThe evaluator additionally runs matched negative controls (permuted outcomes, node-relabelled\n    68\tgraph, constant outcome) through the same operation; a constant-outcome request must\n    69\treturn an estimate within 1e-4 of 0, and the run must be deterministic given the reset seed.\n    70\t\"\"\"\n    71\t\n    72\timport base64\n    73\t\n    74\timport numpy as np\n    75\timport scipy.sparse as sp\n    76\t\n    77\t_STATE = {\"rng\": None, \"seed\": None}\n    78\t\n    79\t_DTYPES = {\"int32\": \"<i4\", \"float64\": \"<f8\", \"uint8\": \"u1\"}\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\tdef decode_array(obj):\n    83\t    \"\"\"Decode an array object (see module docstring) into a numpy array.\"\"\"\n    84\t    if obj is None:\n    85\t        return None\n    86\t    if obj[\"encoding\"] != \"base64-le\" or obj[\"dtype\"] not in _DTYPES:\n    87\t        raise ValueError(\"unsupported array encoding\")\n    88\t    buf = base64.b64decode(obj[\"data\"])\n    89\t    return np.frombuffer(buf, dtype=np.dtype(_DTYPES[obj[\"dtype\"]])).reshape(obj[\"shape\"]).copy()\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\tdef _adjacency(n, edges):\n    93\t    if len(edges) == 0:\n    94\t        return sp.csr_matrix((n, n))\n    95\t    u, v = edges[:, 0], edges[:, 1]\n    96\t    rows = np.concatenate([u, v])\n    97\t    cols = np.concatenate([v, u])\n    98\t    return sp.csr_matrix((np.ones(len(rows)), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n    99\t\n   100\t\n   101\tdef _features(adj, deg, z, x, treated_all):\n   102\t    \"\"\"Design matrix [1, own treatment, neighbour-treated fraction, covariates].\"\"\"\n   103\t    if treated_all is None:\n   104\t        frac = (adj @ z) / np.maximum(deg, 1.0)\n   105\t        own = z\n   106\t    else:\n   107\t        frac = np.where(deg > 0, float(treated_all), 0.0)\n   108\t        own = np.full(len(z), float(treated_all))\n   109\t    return np.column_stack([np.ones(len(z)), own, frac, x])\n   110\t\n   111\t\n   112\tdef _parse(request):\n   113\t    n = int(request[\"n\"])\n   114\t    edges = decode_array(request[\"edges\"])\n   115\t    x = decode_array(request[\"covariates\"])\n   116\t    z = decode_array(request[\"treatment\"]).astype(np.float64)\n   117\t    y = decode_array(request[\"outcomes\"])\n   118\t    adj = _adjacency(n, edges)\n   119\t    deg = np.asarray(adj.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n   120\t    return n, x, z, y, adj, deg\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\tZCRIT = 1.959963984540054  # normal quantile for ci_level = 0.95 (the only level requested)\n   124\t\n   125\t\n   126\tdef _exposure_states(adj, deg, z):\n   127\t    \"\"\"Exposure summaries for the observed, all-treated and all-control worlds.\n   128\t\n   129\t    Two-hop quantities use repeated sparse matrix-vector products only (never adj @ adj).\n   130\t    \"\"\"\n   131\t    n = len(z)\n   132\t    ones = np.ones(n)\n   133\t    walks2 = adj @ (adj @ ones)  # number of length-2 walks starting at each node\n   134\t    s1 = adj @ z\n   135\t    obs = {\n   136\t        \"own\": z,\n   137\t        \"s1\": s1,\n   138\t        \"f1\": s1 / np.maximum(deg, 1.0),\n   139\t        \"f2\": (adj @ (adj @ z)) / np.maximum(walks2, 1.0),\n   140\t    }\n   141\t    all1 = {\n   142\t        \"own\": ones,\n   143\t        \"s1\": deg.astype(np.float64),\n   144\t        \"f1\": (deg > 0).astype(np.float64),\n   145\t        \"f2\": (walks2 > 0).astype(np.float64),\n   146\t    }\n   147\t    all0 = {\"own\": np.zeros(n), \"s1\": np.zeros(n), \"f1\": np.zeros(n), \"f2\": np.zeros(n)}\n   148\t    return obs, all1, all0\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\tdef candidate_designs(deg, x):\n   152\t    \"\"\"Library of few-parameter exposure mappings.\n   153\t\n   154\t    Returns {name: (builder, count_cols)}; builder(state) -> design matrix with columns\n   155\t    [1, own, exposure features..., (x or interactions)].  ``count_cols`` marks columns that\n   156\t    are unbounded treated-neighbour counts (all-treated values get winsorised).\n   157\t    \"\"\"\n   158\t    n = len(deg)\n   159\t    pos = deg[deg > 0]\n   160\t    median_deg = max(float(np.median(pos)), 1.0) if len(pos) else 1.0\n   161\t    mean_deg = max(float(np.mean(deg)), 1.0)\n   162\t    ld = np.log1p(deg)\n   163\t    ldc = ld - ld.mean()\n   164\t    xc = x - x.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n   165\t    one = np.ones(n)\n   166\t\n   167\t    def lin(s):\n   168\t        return np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x])\n   169\t\n   170\t    specs = {\"M0_linear\": (lin, ())}\n   171\t\n   172\t    specs[\"M1_count\"] = (\n   173\t        lambda s: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"s1\"] / mean_deg, x]),\n   174\t        (2,),\n   175\t    )\n   176\t    specs[\"M2_twohop\"] = (\n   177\t        lambda s: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], s[\"f2\"], x]),\n   178\t        (),\n   179\t    )\n   180\t    specs[\"M3_interact\"] = (\n   181\t        lambda s: np.column_stack(\n   182\t            [one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x, ldc, s[\"own\"] * ldc, s[\"own\"] * xc,\n   183\t             s[\"f1\"] * ldc]\n   184\t        ),\n   185\t        (),\n   186\t    )\n   187\t    specs[\"M3b_own_deg_frac_deg\"] = (\n   188\t        lambda s: np.column_stack(\n   189\t            [one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x, ldc, s[\"own\"] * ldc, s[\"f1\"] * ldc]\n   190\t        ),\n   191\t        (),\n   192\t    )\n   193\t    specs[\"M3c_frac_x\"] = (\n   194\t        lambda s: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x, s[\"f1\"] * xc]),\n   195\t        (),\n   196\t    )\n   197\t    for k in (1.0, 3.0, 8.0):\n   198\t        specs[\"M4_sat_k%g\" % k] = (\n   199\t            (lambda s, k=k: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], 1.0 - np.exp(-k * s[\"f1\"]), x])),\n   200\t            (),\n   201\t        )\n   202\t    for t in (0.25, 0.5, 0.75):\n   203\t        specs[\"M5_sig_t%g\" % t] = (\n   204\t            (lambda s, t=t: np.column_stack(\n   205\t                [one, s[\"own\"], 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(s[\"f1\"] - t) / 0.1)), x])),\n   206\t            (),\n   207\t        )\n   208\t    for k in (0.5, 1.0, 2.0):\n   209\t        specs[\"M6_satcount_k%g\" % k] = (\n   210\t            (lambda s, k=k: np.column_stack(\n   211\t                [one, s[\"own\"], 1.0 - np.exp(-s[\"s1\"] / (k * median_deg)), x])),\n   212\t            (),\n   213\t        )\n   214\t    return specs\n   215\t\n   216\t\n   217\tdef sandwich_se(x_obs, resid, contrast, n):\n   218\t    \"\"\"HC1 sandwich delta-method standard error of contrast @ beta.\"\"\"\n   219\t    bread = np.linalg.pinv(x_obs.T @ x_obs)\n   220\t    meat = (x_obs * resid[:, None] ** 2).T @ x_obs\n   221\t    cov = bread @ meat @ bread * n / max(n - x_obs.shape[1], 1)\n   222\t    return float(np.sqrt(max(contrast @ cov @ contrast, 0.0)))\n   223\t\n   224\t\n   225\tdef _fit_candidate(builder, count_cols, states, y):\n   226\t    obs, all1, all0 = states\n   227\t    n = len(y)\n   228\t    x_obs = builder(obs)\n   229\t    x1 = builder(all1)\n   230\t    x0 = builder(all0)\n   231\t    for c in count_cols:  # winsorise count-type all-treated features\n   232\t        cap = 3.0 * float(np.percentile(x_obs[:, c], 99.5))\n   233\t        if cap > 0:\n   234\t            x1[:, c] = np.minimum(x1[:, c], cap)\n   235\t    if not (np.all(np.isfinite(x_obs)) and np.all(np.isfinite(x1)) and np.all(np.isfinite(x0))):\n   236\t        return None\n   237\t    beta, _, rank, _ = np.linalg.lstsq(x_obs, y, rcond=None)\n   238\t    resid = y - x_obs @ beta\n   239\t    rss = float(resid @ resid)\n   240\t    contrast = (x1 - x0).mean(axis=0)\n   241\t    est = float(contrast @ beta)\n   242\t    se = sandwich_se(x_obs, resid, contrast, n)\n   243\t    if not (np.isfinite(est) and np.isfinite(se)):\n   244\t        return None\n   245\t    return {\"est\": est, \"se\": se, \"rss\": rss, \"p\": int(rank)}\n   246\t\n   247\t\n   248\tdef bic_gate(fits, n, y_var, bic_margin=10.0):\n   249\t    \"\"\"Keep the linear fit unless a candidate beats it by BIC > bic_margin.\n   250\t\n   251\t    Passing candidates are averaged with BIC weights.  Returns (est, se, est0, se0).\n   252\t    \"\"\"\n   253\t    base = fits[\"M0_linear\"]\n   254\t    est0, se0 = base[\"est\"], base[\"se\"]\n   255\t    floor = 1e-12 * y_var\n   256\t\n   257\t    def bic(f):\n   258\t        return n * np.log(np.maximum(f[\"rss\"] / n, floor)) + f[\"p\"] * np.log(n)\n   259\t\n   260\t    bic0 = bic(base)\n   261\t    passing = []\n   262\t    for name, f in fits.items():\n   263\t        if name == \"M0_linear\" or f is None:\n   264\t            continue\n   265\t        b = bic(f)\n   266\t        if bic0 - b > bic_margin:\n   267\t            passing.append((b, f))\n   268\t    if not passing:\n   269\t        return est0, se0, est0, se0\n   270\t    bmin = min(b for b, _ in passing)\n   271\t    w = np.array([np.exp(-0.5 * (b - bmin)) for b, _ in passing])\n   272\t    w = w / w.sum()\n   273\t    ests = np.array([f[\"est\"] for _, f in passing])\n   274\t    ses = np.array([f[\"se\"] for _, f in passing])\n   275\t    est = float(w @ ests)\n   276\t    spread = float(np.sqrt(w @ (ests - est) ** 2))\n   277\t    se = float(w @ ses) + spread\n   278\t    # sanity guard: do not stray far from the linear estimate\n   279\t    if abs(est - est0) > 3.0 * max(abs(est0), se0) or not (np.isfinite(est) and np.isfinite(se)):\n   280\t        return est0, se0, est0, se0\n   281\t    return est, se, est0, se0\n   282\t\n   283\t\n   284\tdef _estimate(request):\n   285\t    try:\n   286\t        n, x, z, y, adj, deg = _parse(request)\n   287\t        y_var = float(np.var(y))\n   288\t        if y_var == 0.0:\n   289\t            return {\"estimate\": 0.0, \"ci_low\": 0.0, \"ci_high\": 0.0}\n   290\t        states = _exposure_states(adj, deg, z)\n   291\t        fits = {}\n   292\t        for name, (builder, count_cols) in candidate_designs(deg, x).items():\n   293\t            try:\n   294\t                fits[name] = _fit_candidate(builder, count_cols, states, y)\n   295\t            except Exception:\n   296\t                fits[name] = None\n   297\t        if fits.get(\"M0_linear\") is None:\n   298\t            raise ValueError(\"linear fit failed\")\n   299\t        est, se, est0, se0 = bic_gate(fits, n, y_var, bic_margin=10.0)\n   300\t        half = ZCRIT * se + abs(est - est0)\n   301\t        if not (np.isfinite(est) and np.isfinite(half)):\n   302\t            raise ValueError(\"non-finite\")\n   303\t        return {\"estimate\": est, \"ci_low\": est - half, \"ci_high\": est + half}\n   304\t    except Exception:\n   305\t        return _estimate_linear(request)\n   306\t\n   307\t\n   308\tdef _estimate_linear(request):\n   309\t    n, x, z, y, adj, deg = _parse(request)\n   310\t\n   311\t    x_obs = _features(adj, deg, z, x, None)\n   312\t    beta, *_ = np.linalg.lstsq(x_obs, y, rcond=None)\n   313\t    resid = y - x_obs @ beta\n   314\t    # GATE = mean over nodes of prediction(all treated) - prediction(all control).\n   315\t    contrast = (_features(adj, deg, z, x, 1) - _features(adj, deg, z, x, 0)).mean(axis=0)\n   316\t    est = float(contrast @ beta)\n   317\t\n   318\t    # Heteroskedasticity-robust (HC1) sandwich interval for the linear functional.\n   319\t    bread = np.linalg.pinv(x_obs.T @ x_obs)\n   320\t    meat = (x_obs * resid[:, None] ** 2).T @ x_obs\n   321\t    cov = bread @ meat @ bread * n / max(n - x_obs.shape[1], 1)\n   322\t    se = float(np.sqrt(max(contrast @ cov @ contrast, 0.0)))\n   323\t    zcrit = 1.959963984540054  # normal quantile for ci_level = 0.95 (the only level requested)\n   324\t    return {\"estimate\": est, \"ci_low\": est - zcrit * se, \"ci_high\": est + zcrit * se}\n   325\t\n   326\t\n   327\tdef handle(request):\n   328\t    op = request.get(\"op\")\n   329\t    if op == \"reset\":\n   330\t        seed = int(request[\"seed\"])\n   331\t        _STATE[\"seed\"] = seed\n   332\t        _STATE[\"rng\"] = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n   333\t        return {\"ok\": True}\n   334\t    if op == \"estimate\":\n   335\t        return _estimate(request)\n   336\t    raise ValueError(\"unknown op\")","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
