{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvrCDWP6ki6JMQLCMZ6c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0179rGKEG2vnZoYxU5FQV2RE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\ndef rep(old,new,cnt=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==cnt,(s.count(old),old[:70])\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\n\nrep(r\"when its mapping does or does not match the mechanism, and offer\",\n    r\"when the mechanism is or is not linear in the neighbour-treated fraction, and offer\")\nrep(r\"A graph $G$ on $n=3000$ nodes\", r\"A graph $G$ on $n=3000$ nodes\") \n\n# linear baseline\nrep(r\"\"\"This is the canonical regression GATE estimator \\citep{Chin2018RegressionAF} with a one-hop fraction mapping; it matches the generating form in cases 1--5 up to the own-treatment-by-covariate interaction.\"\"\",\nr\"\"\"This is the canonical regression GATE estimator \\citep{Chin2018RegressionAF} with a one-hop fraction mapping, as implemented by the evaluator (\\texttt{source\\_evidence/evaluator/evaluate.py}, \\texttt{\\_linear\\_features} and \\texttt{\\_ols\\_gate}). Its mapping is linear in the neighbour fraction, as is the generating term in cases 1--5; the generating own-treatment effect also includes a treatment-by-covariate interaction that this regression omits.\"\"\")\n\n# frozen paragraph\na=s.index(r\"\\paragraph{Frozen BIC-gated exposure library (studied estimator).}\")\nb=s.index(r\"\\paragraph{Reference estimators (evaluator-owned).}\")\nnew=r\"\"\"\\paragraph{Frozen BIC-gated exposure library (studied estimator).} The studied estimator (\\texttt{source\\_evidence/frozen\\_estimator/program.py}, functions \\texttt{candidate\\_designs}, \\texttt{bic\\_gate}, \\texttt{\\_estimate}) fits by least squares the linear model above plus 14 alternatives, each with few parameters: a treated-neighbour count divided by the mean degree; a two-hop walk fraction; interactions with log-degree and covariates (three variants); saturating $1-e^{-kf}$ with $k\\in\\{1,3,8\\}$; sigmoids of $f$ centred at $\\{0.25,0.5,0.75\\}$ with scale 0.1; and saturating functions of the count scaled by $\\{0.5,1,2\\}\\times$ the median degree. Exposure features are computed analytically at the observed, all-treated and all-control assignments. In the count mapping only, the all-treated feature is capped at three times the 99.5th percentile of its observed values. An alternative is kept only if its BIC is lower than the linear model's by more than 10; kept alternatives are averaged with BIC weights, and if none passes, or the average departs from the linear estimate by more than three times $\\max(|\\hat\\tau_{\\mathrm{lin}}|,\\mathrm{se}_{\\mathrm{lin}})$, the linear estimate is returned. The interval is $\\hat\\tau\\pm\\big(1.96\\,\\mathrm{se}+|\\hat\\tau-\\hat\\tau_{\\mathrm{lin}}|\\big)$, where $\\mathrm{se}$ is the BIC-weighted mean of HC1 sandwich delta-method standard errors plus the weighted spread of the kept estimates. The estimator is deterministic, reads neither the design description nor the cluster labels, and uses no resampling. It was written after inspecting model-selection results; its per-case gate decisions were not logged in verified form (the evaluation marks candidate diagnostics as unverified), so we cannot report which mapping it selected in any case. In particular, the library contains the exact sigmoid form used to generate case 6 (centre 0.5; steepness 10 corresponds to scale 0.1), so the case-6 error cannot be read as absence of the true form from the library.\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\n\nrep(r\"\"\"\\emph{HT}: a neighbourhood-exposure Horvitz--Thompson estimator that keeps units whose closed neighbourhood is entirely treated (or entirely control) and weights by the design-implied probability of that event. \\emph{Oracle}: OLS with the true exposure mapping for the case plus covariate and own-by-covariate terms; it is a reference for correct specification, not an attainable method.\"\"\",\nr\"\"\"\\emph{HT}: a neighbourhood-exposure Horvitz--Thompson estimator that keeps units whose closed neighbourhood is entirely treated (or entirely control) and weights by the design-implied probability of that event. \\emph{Oracle}: OLS with the true exposure mapping for the case plus covariates and an own-by-covariate term; it is a reference for correct specification, not an attainable method. Definitions follow \\texttt{source\\_evidence/evaluator/evaluate.py} (\\texttt{baseline\\_dim}, \\texttt{baseline\\_ht}, \\texttt{\\_oracle\\_features\\_for}).\"\"\")\nrep(r\"These probe whether the estimator uses graph and outcome structure and whether it is deterministic.\",\n    r\"They are intended to probe whether the estimate reacts to scrambled graph or outcome structure and whether the estimator is deterministic.\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2122,"cache_read_input_tokens":124005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2122},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9055c2ad-8868-47aa-af47-ddab8ec71d32","uuid":"643ad31d-bfdd-450a-a0d8-c32ed3abe87f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:46:42.113Z","request_id":"req_011CgvrCCmV7W22pQudWYrDV"}
