{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvrFjJrd8kD18YCobXSz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mz2FdR6CWEWhKapUxNiwYv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\ndef rep(old,new,cnt=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==cnt,(s.count(old),old[:70])\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\n\nrep(r\"$f^{(2)}$ the two-hop walk fraction (length-two walks from the node that start at a treated node, divided by all length-two walks from the node)\",\n    r\"$f^{(2)}$ the two-hop walk fraction (length-two walks from the node that end at a treated node, divided by all length-two walks from the node, so walks returning to the node are included)\")\nrep(r\"Source: the estimator source file of the frozen estimator, functions \\texttt{candidate\\_designs}, \\texttt{bic\\_gate} and \\texttt{\\_estimate}.\",\n    r\"Source: \\texttt{source\\_evidence/frozen\\_estimator/program.py} (\\texttt{\\_exposure\\_states}, \\texttt{candidate\\_designs}, \\texttt{\\_fit\\_candidate}, \\texttt{bic\\_gate}, \\texttt{\\_estimate}).\")\nrep(r\"saturating-count $[1,z,1-e^{-s/(k\\,\\mathrm{med}_d)},x]$.\", r\"saturating-count $[1,z,1-e^{-s/(k\\,\\mathrm{med}_d)},x]$, where $\\mathrm{med}_d$ is the median degree over non-isolated nodes; the count mapping uses $s/\\bar d$ with $\\bar d$ the mean degree.\")\nrep(r\"The BIC is $n\\log(\\mathrm{RSS}/n)+p\\log n$ with $p$ the rank of the design.\",\n    r\"The BIC is $n\\log(\\mathrm{RSS}/n)+p\\log n$ with $p$ the rank of the design. The sigmoid with $t=0.5$ and scale 0.1 equals the case-6 generating sigmoid up to the coefficient $\\gamma$, which the regression absorbs.\")\nrep(r\"Reference estimators.} DiM, linear and oracle regressions follow Section~3; HT uses\",\n    r\"Reference estimators.} DiM, linear and oracle regressions follow Section~3 (\\texttt{source\\_evidence/evaluator/evaluate.py}); HT uses\")\nrep(r\"The oracle features are $[1,z,x_1,x_2,zx_1]$ plus the true mapping\",\n    r\"The oracle features are $[1,z,x_1,x_2,zx_1]$ (covariates $x_1,x_2$) plus the true mapping\")\nrep(r\"and the relabelled graph shows that the real topology matters. None of these supports accuracy on its own.\",\n    r\"and the relabelled-graph error (0.627) is far above the headline error of 0.126 and similar to the difference-in-means value. We make no mechanistic claim from these values. None of these supports accuracy on its own.\")\nrep(r\"the permuted-outcome control shows the estimate collapses toward zero when outcomes are unrelated to assignment and graph,\",\n    r\"the permuted-outcome control gives a mean absolute estimate of 0.059 times the true GATE,\")\n\n# model selection subsection\na=s.index(r\"\\subsection{Model-Selection Comparison of Estimator Classes}\")\nb=s.index(r\"\\subsection{Reproducibility Notes}\")\ns=s[:a]+r\"\"\"\\subsection{Model-Selection Comparison of Estimator Classes}\nMain-text Table~\\ref{tab:search} reports the eight model-selection seeds (101--108) on the same eight case specifications. The three estimator classes were each scored once; the final estimator was frozen from this comparison, so these numbers are a selection set, not final evidence. Only the plane-mean scores are used in this paper; per-case, bias, coverage and baseline values for this plane are not reported. The two alternatives, as implemented in \\texttt{source\\_evidence/estimator\\_01/program.py} and \\texttt{source\\_evidence/estimator\\_02/program.py}, are: (i) a flexible ensemble that fits ridge regressions on exposure features, compares candidates by cross-validation and a held-out extrapolation split, averages those within one standard error, and builds an interval from a design-resampling wild block bootstrap; and (ii) a linear-regression estimate plus a shrunk, degree-stratified HT-type residual correction with a design-based variance term. We did not inspect their per-case behaviour, so we offer no explanation for their scores.\n\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\n\nrep(r\"The estimator source file, the evaluator that generates graphs, assignments, outcomes, baselines and controls, the case-specification files for both planes, and \\texttt{build\\_figures.py}, which reads the evidence registry and regenerates Figures~\\ref{fig:main} and~\\ref{fig:rel} and the derived statistics (bootstrap with fixed seed 0), accompany this submission. Table~\\ref{tab:cases} and Table~\\ref{tab:spec} come from the final case-specification file and the evaluator's per-case metrics; Tables~\\ref{tab:seeds}--\\ref{tab:search} come from the per-seed evidence file and the per-plane metric files. Each final seed took about ten seconds on CPU. The final evaluation used seeds 9001--9024; model selection used 101--108. Software versions are recorded in the accompanying task requirements file and are not restated here.\",\n    r\"The directory \\texttt{source\\_evidence/} holds the three estimator source files (\\texttt{frozen\\_estimator}, \\texttt{estimator\\_01}, \\texttt{estimator\\_02}), the evaluator scripts for the two planes, both case-specification files and the evaluator's requirements file (numpy 2.2.6, scipy 1.15.3, scikit-learn 1.6.1, networkx 3.4.2). \\texttt{build\\_figures.py} reads the evidence registry and regenerates Figures~\\ref{fig:main} and~\\ref{fig:rel} and the derived statistics (bootstrap with fixed seed 0). Table~\\ref{tab:cases} and Table~\\ref{tab:spec} come from the final case-specification file and the evaluator's per-case metrics; Table~\\ref{tab:seeds} comes from the per-seed evidence file; Table~\\ref{tab:search} uses the plane scores of the three model-selection runs. Each final seed took about ten seconds on CPU. The final evaluation used seeds 9001--9024; model selection used 101--108.\")\nrep(r\"The estimator's per-case behaviour was not inspected beyond the recorded metrics, as noted in the limitations.\",\n    r\"The estimator's per-case behaviour and mapping choices were not inspected beyond the recorded metrics, as noted in the limitations.\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"Section~3\" paper.tex | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2552,"cache_read_input_tokens":131158,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2552},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9055c2ad-8868-47aa-af47-ddab8ec71d32","uuid":"145931a8-ae37-4318-80ec-e7aa801431ad","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:47:30.447Z","request_id":"req_011CgvrFiR2h9PKwWE5y1TU8"}
